    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Sofia's Photography Webpage\r\n\r\nSofia wants to make a webpage about her photography hobby but doesn't know how to write HTML or CSS. Instead, they've provided you with a description and a potential screenshot:\r\n\r\n> \"I want to make a webpage about my photography because I want to share my work and tell people a little about how I got into it. I want the title to be big and bold with a line under it. And I want the photos to look like they're in a frame - like something you'd hang on a wall.\"\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/2a914c0a73a73a185f4d548bb8523cf0-image-1774476705361.png\" style=\"width: 40%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1) Use AI tutor to help build this page. Ask it to make changes to this page step-by-step.\r\n    - Be specific about the elements, sizes, borders, and which elements they apply to\r\n2) Keep prompting until the webpage it's \"close enough\" to their vision!\r\n    - It doesn't have to perfectly match the image, but try to get it close to the style and layout!\r\n\r\nOnce you've compared your result to Sofia's vision: press the Continue button!\r\n\r\n**Hint:** This puzzle involves `<img>` and `<h1>` tags in HTML, and the `border` and `text-decoration` properties in CSS.\r\n\r\n![]()",
